Modifications (Apache License 2.0, section 4(b)):
  Only frames 217 and 226 were kept: the two NTPv4 client requests from
  2001:bef::a00:27ff:fe0d:5c3c:123 to 2001:418:8405:4002::3:123 and to
  2001:67c:1560:8003::c8:123. The pcap file header and both records,
  including timestamps, are byte-for-byte unchanged:

    editcap -F pcap -r ospf.pcap ja4n-arkime-ospf-ipv6.pcap 217 226

  Result: 276 bytes, SHA-256
  eb27bbc5ba5acfb45ad3712bbed0bd68228708b7250f6427e0c773116d7b1317.

Use:
  zeek/testing/tests/ja4n-ospf-ipv6-arkime-golden.zeek, against the
  "ntp.ja4n" values Arkime recorded for these sessions in arkime/ja4
  pcap/ospf.test, commit 27099fb11f351f35d69f4ce366374aa91536af04
  (SHA-256 d1f9862ec1af9efcefdd24dff3f99cc68da5608e4b6f862a06e62f2afcd0177a).
